8,"y":2824,"w":1780,"h":44}]},{"page":4,"width":2436,"height":3156,"lines":[{"text":"Argument Against","x":1057,"y":267,"w":344,"h":43},{"text":"East Palo Alto $125,000,000 Bond Issue, Measure","x":743,"y":317,"w":914,"h":39},{"text":"When voters are asked to go into debt with bond measures like Measure","x":373,"y":415,"w":1252,"h":42},{"text":"what are they saying?","x":1704,"y":418,"w":374,"h":41},{"text":"They are admitting that everything in the current budget is more ilnportant than the projects listed","x":371,"y":466,"w":1697,"h":44},{"text":"in this ballot measure.","x":372,"y":516,"w":382,"h":33},{"text":"Budgets reflect priorities. Actions speak louder than words: every tax dollar spent today is","x":369,"y":618,"w":1673,"h":43},{"text":"going to something they consider a higher priority than \"replacing deteriorating water","x":370,"y":668,"w":1603,"h":43},{"text":"pipes to provide safe/ clean drinking water\" and \"constructing a Library.\"","x":370,"y":719,"w":1380,"h":43},{"text":"Do you agree?","x":366,"y":819,"w":265,"h":41},{"text":"A bond is much like a mortgage. When you buy a home, truth in lending laws mandate that","x":367,"y":918,"w":1601,"h":44},{"text":"banks must tell the real cost (the loan amount AND 30 years of interest payments).","x":367,"y":969,"w":1440,"h":44},{"text":"$ 125,000,000 could cost us $250,000,000 or more (depending on the interests' rates).","x":367,"y":1069,"w":1487,"h":44},{"text":"Shouldn't consumer protection laws apply to bond debt too? We deserve to know the full truth","x":367,"y":1170,"w":1658,"h":44},{"text":"about Measure . We don't even know when this debt will begin, nor what market interest rate","x":365,"y":1221,"w":1670,"h":42},{"text":"will be, when it does.","x":365,"y":1271,"w":372,"h":38},{"text":"Shouldn't consumer protection laws apply to bond measures? Taxpayers deserve all the full facts.","x":366,"y":1371,"w":1698,"h":45},{"text":"We do not know when this debt will begin, or what the market interest rate will be at that time.","x":365,"y":1422,"w":1649,"h":42},{"text":"Which is more important to you?","x":363,"y":1519,"w":619,"h":42},{"text":"1. Paying for essential safety repairs u,g_!!, by using dollars already in the budgetl.","x":363,"y":1620,"w":1480,"h":43},{"text":"2. Sending new tax dollars in the form of principal and interest paynwnts -- to big banks,","x":360,"y":1721,"w":1657,"h":43},{"text":"investment brokers, and other wealthy people, for use in tax shelters.","x":435,"y":1772,"w":1226,"h":44},{"text":"Is #2 really the best use of our taxes?","x":361,"y":1873,"w":694,"h":40},{"text":"If you value clean drinking water more than funding tax shelters with tax free bonds, vote","x":361,"y":1974,"w":1667,"h":43},{"text":"NO on Measure","x":360,"y":2025,"w":297,"h":33},{"text":"If you value clean water more than making interest payments for 25 years, vote NO on","x":360,"y":2126,"w":1614,"h":44},{"text":"Measure","x":360,"y":2177,"w":164,"h":32},{"text":"More information, www.SVTaxpayers.org","x":359,"y":2278,"w":746,"h":43},{"text":"FILED","x":976,"y":2471,"w":94,"h":33},{"text":"OF THE CHIEF ELECTIONS OFFICER","x":794,"y":2518,"w":591,"h":38},{"text":"9","x":2229,"y":1303,"w":20,"h":46},{"text":"6","x":2215,"y":1513,"w":43,"h":55},{"text":"1","x":2197,"y":1862,"w":32,"h":63},{"text":"3","x":2197,"y":2038,"w":32,"h":46},{"text":"zee","x":2098,"y":2499,"w":177,"h":72},{"text":"SAN MATEO COUNTY","x":850,"y":2570,"w":347,"h":35},{"text":"AUG II 2026","x":891,"y":2684,"w":263,"h":48},{"text":"BY:","x":657,"y":2873,"w":51,"h":37},{"text":"DEPUT CLERK","x":894,"y":2922,"w":258,"h":34},{"text":"FFICER","x":1268,"y":2799,"w":120,"h":34}]}]}
